# Input
```svelte
<!-- should generate diagnostics -->

<script module>
	export const RADIO = "radio";
</script>

<script>
	const kind = "checkbox";
	const type = "checkbox";
	const radio = RADIO;
	let checked = $state(false);
</script>

<input type={"checkbox"} bind:value={checked} />
<input type={kind} bind:value={checked} />
<input {type} bind:value={checked} />
<input type={`check${"box"}`} bind:value={checked} />
<input type={radio} bind:value={checked} />
{#if checked}
	{@const local = "radio"}
	<input type={local} bind:value={checked} />
{/if}

```

# Diagnostics
```
invalidConstantType.svelte:14:26 lint/nursery/noSvelteBindValueOnCheckableInputs  FIXABLE  ━━━━━━━━━━

  × bind:value does not track whether this checkbox is checked.
  
    12 │ </script>
    13 │ 
  > 14 │ <input type={"checkbox"} bind:value={checked} />
       │                          ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
    15 │ <input type={kind} bind:value={checked} />
    16 │ <input {type} bind:value={checked} />
  
  i Users change whether a checkbox is checked, not its value.
  
  i Use bind:checked to track whether this checkbox is checked, or bind:group to track the values of all checked checkboxes in a group.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  
  i Unsafe fix: Use bind:checked instead.
  
    12 12 │   </script>
    13 13 │   
    14    │ - <input·type={"checkbox"}·bind:value={checked}·/>
       14 │ + <input·type={"checkbox"}·bind:checked={checked}·/>
    15 15 │   <input type={kind} bind:value={checked} />
    16 16 │   <input {type} bind:value={checked} />
  

```

